================================================================================
7. CREATE THE FETCH FUNCTION
================================================================================

const URL =
  'https://www.googleapis.com/books/v1/volumes?q=javascript';


const fetchBooks = async () => {

  try {

    const response = await fetch(URL);

    const data = await response.json();

    const bookList = data.items || [];

    setBooks(bookList);

  } catch (error) {

    console.error('Error fetching books:', error);

  }

};


HOW IT WORKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. fetch(URL)

   Sends HTTP request to the API.


2. await

   Waits for the asynchronous operation to complete.


3. response.json()

   Converts the API response into JavaScript data.


4. data.items

   Gets the books array.


5. data.items || []

   Returns an empty array if items does not exist.


6. setBooks(bookList)

   Stores fetched books in React state.


